#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
VELVET · velvet-books

Velly's book studio: whole paperbacks for Amazon KDP — the interior PDF, the
full-wrap cover, the listing (title, description, seven keywords, categories,
price), a review page and an upload checklist. She makes them at night (bin/
velvet-night); you look them over and upload them — KDP has no upload API,
and the account is yours.

    velvet-books status                  the shelf and the studio, JSON
    velvet-books new [KIND] [--idea TEXT] [--lang de|en] [--audience kids|adults|seniors]
                                         start a book. KIND: coloring | puzzle | picture
                                         (picture needs the picture engine — see `engine`)
    velvet-books work [--minutes N] [--book ID] [--until-done]
                                         the next steps of the open books, one at a time;
                                         every step is saved, so a stop loses at most one picture
    velvet-books list                    every book, one line each
    velvet-books shelf                   the shelf's folder in the file manager
    velvet-books show ID                 one book: where it is, what it needs, its listing
    velvet-books open ID                 its review page in the browser
    velvet-books redo ID [--page N | --cover | --listing | --all]
    velvet-books uploaded ID [--asin X]  you put it on KDP: it leaves the "to upload" pile
    velvet-books engine [setup]          the picture engine (stable-diffusion.cpp + Z-Image-Turbo):
                                         what is there, and — only with `setup`, started by you —
                                         the download (~7 GB) with its sources and sizes
    velvet-books --selftest

Kinds, and what each needs:
  coloring  50 mandalas, single-sided, 8.5 × 11 in, black ink — nothing to download
  puzzle    sudoku, word searches and mazes with solutions, 8.5 × 11 in — nothing to download
  picture   a story picture book, 8.5 × 8.5 in, full colour with bleed — the local brain
            writes and edits the story, the picture engine paints it

What a book becomes on disk: ~/Dokumente/Velly Bücher/<nr> <title>/ — book.json (the
state), interior.pdf, cover.pdf, cover-front.jpg, listing.txt, review.html,
CHECKLIST.md. The KDP numbers (sizes, bleed, spine, print cost, royalty) were
read from KDP's help pages on 2026-10-23; the checklist says to check them in
KDP's own calculator before you set the price.
"""

import datetime
import fcntl
